WEBVTT

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.450
Meta-body loss rate, 2.4 percent.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.930
The reconstruction program is running,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.840
but we can't keep up with the rate of decay.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.270
Loss rate now 2.8 percent!

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.940
Activate all backup programs!

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.600
Save the commander, whatever it takes!

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.270
Loss rate now over three percent.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.180
Any more decay and meta-body
reconstruction will be impossible.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.110
Stop! I'm begging you, please stop!

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.850
Leave this to me.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.280
You...

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.050
What's wrong?

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.710
What the!

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.320
A large-scale deutera zone has
begun to activate in the Arctic.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.390
Judging from its energy level,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.330
we believe it will grow into
a super-sized deutera zone...

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.130
that will envelop the entire Earth.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.930
The Gards-orm stole the first move from us?!

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.500
Oh, no... If the deutera zone
envelops the entire Earth,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.230
it'll completely change the
composition of the atmosphere.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.340
Even if humanity is resurrected,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.900
we wouldn't be able
to live on Earth anymore!

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.040
How long until the deutera is complete?

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.040
23 hours, 46 minutes, 52 seconds.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.250
That's how long mankind has to live, huh?

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.930
We managed to stop the decay.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.320
He's stable for now, but... But...

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.230
We can't wake him up.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.240
What the hell happened to him?!

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.840
His life span.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.070
What do you mean?

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.010
He's special.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.790
Tell me!

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.280
What do you mean
the commander is "special"?

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.160
All right.
He intended to tell you everything.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.660
<i>All of you, listen as well. Shima...</i>

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.700
isn't a normal meta-body.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.780
He's a clone. A meta-body clone.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.710
A meta-body clone?!

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:06.770
Shima's real form is elsewhere.
He's just a part of it.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:14.020
<i>You can't copy the quantum data of</i>
<i>a meta-body, so he created a clone.</i>

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.390
<i>No...</i>

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:19.920
<i>You can't do that!</i>

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.090
No, you can. Or rather, <i>they</i> can.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.670
"They"? You don't mean!

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:30.840
Time is accelerated
within the Gards-orm server.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.400
Science advances much faster
compared to humanity.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.210
The Gards-orm?

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.580
Then, the commander is?!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.740
<i>While he is Gards-orm,</i>
<i>he's someone who turned against Naga.</i>

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.110
It can't be! I don't believe it!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.450
But it's the truth.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.930
However, in order
to help mankind,

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.400
he needed to stay
with the Gards-orm.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:56.500
And so he created a clone of himself...

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.660
from ruined meta-body data that
floated like flotsam in the quantum sea,

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.760
and then inserted it into a human server.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.040
The Oceanus was originally
Gards-orm technology.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.500
Shima, with the twelve other
commanders, developed the Zegapain.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.650
Armor of light to encase the meta-bodies
who had lost it and allow them to fight.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.780
The holonic loader is his
conceptualization of that.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:25.690
But, in the end,
he was based on corrupted data.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.930
<i>Without the regulation system</i>
<i>of the dummy Maihama server...</i>

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:33.160
<i>to provide periodic maintenance,</i>
<i>he can't maintain his meta-body.</i>

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.660
<i>And now he's reached his limit.</i>

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:42.150
That's what you meant by his
"family doctor" and his life span?

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.710
Seriously?

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.680
Why?

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.310
Why do you know so much?!
Shizuno, are one of them, too?!

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.680
<i>No.</i>

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.510
<i>I'm not one of the Gards-orm.</i>

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.520
I believe her!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.100
<i>She'd never lie to us.</i>

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.900
<i>Besides, if she was a Gards-orm agent,</i>

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.100
<i>the Oceanus would have</i>
<i>been shot down long ago!</i>

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.710
He has a point.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.970
She's had no reason to let us live till now.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.820
<i>Thank you, Kyo.</i>

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.050
Let's be reborn into humans!

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.450
The president and you and everyone else!

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:27.620
That goes without saying.
We have no other choice now.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.230
So, what are you gonna do?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.900
If what Commander Shima said is true,

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.830
the Gards-orm aren't going to
turn us into Reconstructants.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:39.970
I'll fight.

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:43.430
If there's no other way to survive,
then even I'll do it!

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.910
All right! That's that!

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.610
Shima is?!

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.740
I see. Then what about the
plan to resurrect mankind?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.950
Don't worry. I'll direct it in his place.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.660
<i>Can you do it, Minato?</i>

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:01.280
He's the one who found
and awakened me.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.260
I want to help him any way I can!
Besides...

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.870
We have a fine crew on the Oceanus...

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.660
who can help an inexperienced
commander like me.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.560
<i>I envy the crew you've been blessed with.</i>

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.110
All right, Vice-Commander Minato.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.810
Study the mission diagram at once...

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.150
<i>and complete the switch over to</i>
<i>the command system it lays out.</i>

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:24.580
Aye!

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:26.850
<i>Do you think you'll be ready?</i>

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:27.820
We will.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.020
Say, Lu-shen...

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.960
What are your dreams for the future?

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:41.530
When I was a kid, I always
loved those hero shows on TV.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:47.540
I seriously thought that, when I grew up,
I'd transform into a hero and fight bad guys.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:52.980
That's why, when Shizuno-sempai called
to me and I rode in the Zega that first time,

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.880
I didn't mind.
Honestly, I was a little happy about it.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.780
The fact it wasn't my first time
doesn't really matter.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.750
What I wanted to be...

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.920
Oh, yeah!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.390
When this operation's over
and we're all resurrected,

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.880
I'll introduce you to my friends.
They're great people!

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:16.760
It might be a little hard explaining
the situation to them, but...

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.990
Hell, I bet they'll understand.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.170
And then we'll all go swimming!
In the real ocean!

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.700
That's a promise, Lu-shen.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:32.810
- Isn't he adorable?
- Yes, he is! Blub! Blub! Blub! Drink it all up!

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.540
Pieta!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.420
He makes promises without even
knowing if he can do it or not.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.060
He doesn't even question himself about it.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:42.790
That's his determination.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.750
Kyo always assumes
he's going to make it back alive.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:49.400
We can't predict what'll
happen in the next second.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.770
Let alone what our future holds.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.830
That's why Kyo always gives every task his all.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.770
He always looks ahead.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.180
You and Kyo really do belong together.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.310
Why do you say that?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.840
I want Kyo to be happy.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.380
I want him to live with the one he loves.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.650
I think you've misunderstood something.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.620
It's true that I still love Kyo.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:16.090
But I don't plan on taking the
same road through life with him.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.360
No... I can't walk that path.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:21.930
How can you be so certain?

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:23.390
Because...

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.800
Because... I am Yehl.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.840
Vice-Commander, it's time.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.890
Where is this place?!

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.390
It's my city... but it's NOT!

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.800
Will you come with me?

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.720
I'm going now, Commander.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.960
Deutera zone expansion
rate now plus three.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:29.870
Time remaining until complete coverage
of the Earth is now 17 hours, 43 minutes!

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.690
All ships, fully deployed!
All systems, on-line!

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:36.230
Countdown running!
20 seconds to mission start!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.720
Captain, I'll need your help for this.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:46.480
Aye.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.450
Mission start in ten seconds.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.250
Nine...

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.180
Eight...

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:51.080
Seven...

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:52.290
Six...

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.320
Five seconds.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.090
Four...

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.020
Three...

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:55.920
Two...

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:56.960
One!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.720
Set course for the
Gards-orm Arctic core server!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.430
Oceanus, launch!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:28.160
Our final operation,
Project Resurrection,

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.090
has been organized into four phases.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.730
First, phase one.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.330
At the start of the mission,

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.200
all ships simultaneously
advance on the Arctic.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.870
Since the enemy's giant deutera zone,
which the Gards-orm call "Sabato,"

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:44.780
has already spread to
the periphery of the Arctic,

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.180
all ships will climb
to their designated altitude...

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.940
and then mass together into formation.

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.880
We'll take a ballistic orbit for the shortest...

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.150
and fastest approach to
the enemy core server.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:59.290
The fleet will launch an all-out attack
on the Gards-orm defense line...

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.830
set up at the Arctic Circle as a diversion.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:06.520
We'll use this gap to penetrate their
defense line and enter Sabato.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.830
Due to the effect of the deutera zone,

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.540
the current Arctic weather
conditions are unstable.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.140
I can't make any forecasts.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.830
At that point, we move to mission phase two.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:20.110
In order to stop any further
impingement by Sabato,

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:23.770
the diversion fleet will attack the Arctic
core server with Zegapain teams.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:26.780
However, the Dvaraka will
withdraw from the battle line...

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.950
and proceed on its own to satellite orbit...

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:33.010
to attack the Gards-orm orbital base
"Cloud" and cut off any reinforcements.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:35.530
While it's doing that,

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:38.430
the Oceanus will take control of the giant
quantum portal in the enemy facility...

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:42.460
and use it to quantum teleport to
the enemy lunar base G-Phaetus.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.940
Take the Oceanus itself to the moon?!

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.430
Their lunar defense line is perfect.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:49.910
The human forces can't
approach it from the outside.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.700
There's no other way
for us to invade G-Phaetus.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.310
After we arrive at the moon,
we proceed to phase three.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.680
That's when you and
the Zegas take the stage.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.190
At last!

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.760
Don't say that you've
found your place to die.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.420
Don't worry.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:11.050
If I die now, I don't know what
I'd say to Arque in the afterlife.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.130
We're going to be reborn.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:14.930
We're not leaving even one person behind.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.340
The Zega team will repel the enemy...

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:21.130
and make contact with our
agent within G-Phaetus itself.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.370
Agent?

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:27.040
Correct. Commander Shima's original.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.980
He's waiting for the Oceanus to arrive...

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.740
so he can complete the
resurrection system for humanity.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:37.780
The moment we obtain the system,
we'll recover the Maihama server.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.750
And that takes us to
the fourth and final phase.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:43.460
We destroy G-Phaetus's main server.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.760
In short, crush the head of the snake...

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.530
and kill the Gards-orm
at the source, right?

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:51.800
After that, the Oceanus returns to Earth.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.910
The mission will require
15 hours to complete.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:59.340
The mission should be finished before the
deutera zone completely engulfs the Earth.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:03.480
In the event Sabato is still active
after G-Phaetus is destroyed,

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.110
we will support our allied vessels.

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:09.950
No matter what the outcome,
we foresee an inevitable enemy attack.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.080
Be ready for it. That is all.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:13.690
Understand?

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:15.230
I understand fine.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:20.130
Basically, this is a reckless operation
with almost no chance of success, right?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.130
Listen, you!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.500
He's right. This plan is for the
resurrection of the human race.

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.840
But it's unexpectedly turned
into our final operation.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.410
Even so...

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.250
It's reckless,
but our chances aren't zero.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:39.050
If you wish to survive, then open the way
to a new destiny with your own hands.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.240
That's what the Prez would've said, right?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:43.990
You're right.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:48.290
So long as we still have some chance,
we can't give up!

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:52.720
Then let's beat these Gards-orm and
take back our future from them!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.490
Vice-Commander, the fleet has
arrived at the Arctic Circle.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.530
All hands, battle stations!

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.930
900 seconds to contact
with Gards-orm defense line!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.740
Warning sensor reaction!
We've been picked up on enemy radar!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.650
At last! At last! What we've waited for!

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:15.140
The lightless ones who must
be wiped away are coming!

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:19.180
We must fill the world with Naga's light.

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:22.790
An eternal light which will
never be extinguished!

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:26.490
Prep for anti-air battle!
Deploy G.A.S.P.R. cannon!

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:30.970
<i>Gravity Acceleration System</i>
<i>Powered Railgun, ready for launch.</i>

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.970
All ships, synched and ready!

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:36.410
Trigger timing has been
transferred to this vessel!

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.500
Enemy mobile forces, detected!
Initiating targeting alignment!

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.610
Releasing locks on all systems!

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.170
All ships have completed pre-fire sequence!

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.690
We can attack at any time!

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:15.310
18 seconds to contact with enemy mobile forces!

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.110
Message from the Deukalion!

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.180
<i>Commander Isola!</i>

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:19.350
Where's the Oceanus?

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.440
Bearing to 8 o'clock, range: nineteen thousand!

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.150
Enemy defense line contact in 120 seconds!

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.660
<i>Commander Isola, we have to return fire!</i>

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.590
Have you forgotten, Commander Ile?

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.460
Our job is to open a path out to space.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.860
We have to draw the enemy in
till the very last second!

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.400
The fleet!

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.960
Oceanus now 30 seconds
from enemy defense line!

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:44.870
All right! Now! All ships, FIRE!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.650
All Zegapain units, scramble!

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.860
<i>Transmission port energy compilation at 98%!</i>

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.660
<i>Transmission scatter rate, green!</i>

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:07.100
<i>E.X. condition, green! All clear!</i>

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.330
<i>Zegapain, transmit!</i>

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.560
Entangle!

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:15.870
Enemy mobile forces ahead
of us have been wiped out!

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:17.540
The diversion was a success.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.630
Maintain course!
We'll break through in one move!

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.340
Residual enemy forces closing from 9 o'clock!

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.920
Get going, Oceanus!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.630
Vice-Commander!

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:43.300
Shouldn't we go out, too?!

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.960
<i>We have to breach their defense line first!</i>

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:55.850
An ambush?!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.580
Identified! Nautilus! Too many to count!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.110
Prep for cannon and torpedo attack!
Anti-air cannons, FIRE!

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.030
Who's in that Zega?!

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.790
It's Toga and Meivelle from the Dvaraka!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.040
Toga! Behind us!

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:28.810
What?!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.020
The Altair has initiated its launch sequence!

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.250
What?!

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>We can't let ourselves get shot down here!</i>

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.430
Let's go, Kaminagi!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.460
Right!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.290
Entangle!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.010
Shit!

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:03.710
Who did that?!

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:04.810
You okay?!

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.710
Kyo Sogoru and Ryoko Kaminagi
from the Oceanus?

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.590
You idiots!

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:13.390
What's the point of this diversion if you
guys launch?! Get back to your ship!

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:15.920
I know, but if the ship
goes down here, it's all over!

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:19.550
There's no way I'm letting that happen!
Don't you trust me?!

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.490
I've never even met you!

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:29.030
Besides, I don't like having someone
sacrificing themselves on our account!

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.840
You wanna make all our
hard work be for nothing?!

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.140
When I get my body back,
I'm gonna kick your sorry ass!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.070
Who's gonna kick whose ass?!

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.950
As much as I damn well want to!

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.920
Oh, yeah?! Let's see you try!

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:44.210
Um, Kyo?
Are we here to fight or to argue?

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:49.060
You're as good as I've heard.
Not bad, Kyo Sogoru.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:53.320
And the legendary Wizard Witch,
Ryoko Kaminagi. You, too.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:56.500
Oh! Sure!
So are you, Toga and Meivelle.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.900
<i>There's no end to them!</i>
<i>Hey! Kyo Sogoru!</i>

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:02.270
<i>Give us all the Q.L. you've got!</i>

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.640
What?!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.010
<i>I'll take them on all at once!</i>
<i>Use that chance and go!</i>

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:10.910
Understood.

00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.820
<i>Q.L. charging, complete!</i>

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.130
Meivelle!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.520
Leave it to me!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.160
Holonic field, forming.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.860
Holo-Bolt Gravity!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.260
SUCK ON THIS!!!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.450
Flight path is clear! Now's our chance!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.210
Oceanus, ahead full!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.890
Thanks for the helping hand.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.450
Kyo Sogoru, next time we meet,
I promise I'll pay you back for it.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:58.790
Next time. I swear it.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:04.160
They do well,
despite being lightless ones.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.130
We'll go out as well.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.060
<i>Thirteen hours left.</i>

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:11.470
<i>Good luck to you.</i>

00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:54.240
Acting as a shield for the Oceanus, becoming decoys,

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:56.810
one comrade after another becomes a sacrifice.

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:59.350
The quantum portal, the doorway to G-Phaetus...

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:01.870
At last, the time has come to
return to the moon, hasn't it?

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:05.490
Why are Abyss and Sin doing that themselves?!

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:08.390
What's this enormous Q.L. reaction we're detecting?

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:11.320
No, wait... That's not the Coatlicue!

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:15.200
Next time, on Zegapain: "The Unsinking Moon."

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:18.030
My pain, never to be forgotten.
